************************************************************************ Dialog Manager Version 3.3** Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1986-1993* All rights reserved.*** Originally by Jean-Charles Mourey* Modified by Harry Yee** The dialog manager is a tool that supports modal and modeless * dialogs.** Files:*    Special.Macros** Modification History** Version 1.3** January 16, 1987	               Steven Glass** The User Control DefProc was always dereferencing the control and* setting the port.	 Even when the RecSize message was being sent.* This is not allowed.  Very bad!** January 28, 1987	               Steven Glass** I found that the LineEdit defproc had	the same problem as	above.* It always set the	port and origin even for the RecSize message.** Jim Merrit also reported a bug in SetDAFont which seemed to be* caused by the storeLONGinZP routine.	The routine was only* storing the first	word of the long rather than the whole thing.** VERSION 2.0** April 20, 1987	                Dan	Hitchens** A new item type, LongStatText2, was incorporated into the	Dialog* manager.  Its Itemtype=22 and its PartCode=15.** A bug in IsDialogEvent which allowed it to claim all update and* activate events was fixed. It now functions correctly by only* claiming those activate and update events which occur in a dialog* window.** VERSION 2.X** November xx,1987	                 Dan Hitchens** A bug in GetNewXXX with a refcon value of non-zero would cause a crash* or unpredictable results was fixed.** A bug with IsDialogEvent which didn't allow it to claim the following* events: WInDrag, WInGrow, WInGoAway, WInZoom, WInInfo, WInVerScrl,* WInHorScrl, WInFrame, WinDrop.*** Version 2.1	Harry Yee** February 1988** Code modified to build under MAX.** Code modified to avoid using in line storage so it should work in * ROM.** March 4, 1988** Code re-formatted and entabbed.** March 28, 1988	Harry Yee	v2.2d1** DisableDItem/EnableDItem call, when passed an invalid ID item number, would fail because* it did not clean up the stack correctly when exiting. The enable/disable flag was left* on the stack.  This has been fixed ** May 2, 1988	Harry Yee	v2.2d2 (for System Disk 3.2d21)** HideDItem/ShowDItem, GetDItemValue, when passed an invalid ID item number, would fail* because it did not clean up the stack correctly when exiting.  This has been fixed** May 9, 1988       Harry Yee	v2.2d3 (for System Disk 3.2d22)** Problem with using the special paramtext indicators "^0" to "^3" when they are used as * the last character on a line.  An extra garbage char. is printed out along with the* string.  In the procedure InsertParamString the length byte DestLen was being incremented* by one too many when the procedure exited causing _LETextBox to print out one to many* characters. This has been fixed.** May 16, 1988	Harry Yee	v2.2d4 (for System Disk 3.2d23)** The following calls: GetDItemType, SetDItemType, SetDItemValue, when passed an* invalid ID item number, would fail because it did not clean up the stack correctly* when exiting. This has been fixed in the routines GetItemWord, SetItemWord, and* SetDItemValue respectively.** May 27, 1988	Harry Yee	v2.2d5 (for System Disk 3.2d25)** Fixed DialogStatus call. After calling DialogShutDown and then calling DialogStatus, * DialogStatus would always return non-zero, meaning it was still active.*** 07 Jun 88	Harry and Steve	v 2.2d5 (for System Disk 3.2d26)** The StatText, LongStatText LineEdit drawing routines assumed the foreground* and background colors in the GrafPort were correctly set.  This was* only the case if other controls in the dialog had been colored and * had been drawn first.** 15 Jun 88	Harry Yee** Prototype bit taken out of TheDialogVersionNum for final release.** 13 Jul 88	Harry Yee	v2.3d1 (for System Disk 4.0d11)** IsDialogEvent is capturing too many taskmaster events. wInContent * should be the only one that causes IsDialogEvent to return True. This * undoes the change from November xx, 1987 by Dan Hitchens.** Handle for memory obtained during DialogStartup for the window parameters was* being locked down until DialogShutDown was called which disposed of the handle.* The handle is now created with no restrictions and locked down and dereferenced* when used and then unlocked when its not (this handle is only accessed in routine* NewDialog).  The UserID was also incorrect for the memory obtained. I now use* what was passed to me in ProgramID.** 26 Jul 88	Harry Yee	v2.3d2 (for System Disk 4.0d14)** Having a paramtext string of length zero inserts two bytes of garbage in* the output string. Fix was in routine InsertParamString.  When a paramtext* indicator ^n was encountered we were not checking for a zero length string.* Therefore we were always writing at least two bytes of garbage into the* output string.** 04 Aug 88	Harry Yee	v2.3d3 (for System Disk 4.0d16)** Routine Long_Call did not RTL to the correct location if the address of the routine* was located at the very beginning of a bank (i.e. n/0000). Long_call used to * decrement the data bank also if the low word of the address was zero. We now no* longer touch the data bank, and only decrement the low word.** 07 Oct 88	Steven Glass	v2.4 for v4.1d2 and RevD03** The StatText, LongStatText and Icon DefProcs were always dereferencing * the control and doing other setup...	even when the RecSize message * was being sent.** 02 Dec 88	Harry Yee	v2.4 for v4.1d5 disk and RevD07** Fixed bug in GetNextDItem (BRC #38734). Only the low word of the handle to* the next control was being used. Also was not checking for end of control list.** 19 May 89	Steven Glass** Change to DialogStart to ignore previous state.  Should help* Mavis Beacon keep running.** 9/7/89	Mensch* Changed a handle allocation to allocate a fixed handle, this prevents the * dialog manager writing over someone else's memory.** 11/13/89	Mensch** Fixed modal dialog so that it does not suck off app events BRC#53469** 17-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Removed dependency on all.macros.* Crunched "pushlong <xxx" and "pushword <xxx" macros to pushlongdp and pushworddp.* Optimizations (search for DAL).* Version number $8304.* This saved 362 bytes for ROM 1.** 24-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Changed link and tlink macros to omit useless "sec sbc #0 tcs" after a tsc.* Changed StdSoundProc to call SysBeep2 with $8000 for Alert stage 0,* 1-3 for Alert stages 1-3, and 4 for clicking outside a dialog or alert.** 17-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Changed StdSoundProc again to use the newly-defined bit 14 in SysBeep2, to* defer the sound until the next GetNextEvent call.  Click-outside-dialog is* not deferred, but the other ones are.** 3-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed a very old coding error after GetOldEditLine; it was checking the low* word of a value twice instead of checking both words.  I don't think this* had any actual consequences, but I fixed it anyway.** 5-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Adding support for I-Beam cursors.  Set bit 30 of the ModalDialog or* ModalDialog2 filter proc, and it calls InitCursor for you on the way in.* Then it watches where the cursor is and calls InitCursor and IBeamCursor* for you, and it resets the cursor to an arrow on the way out if* necessary.** 7-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Rewrote part of the I-Beam stuff.  Now uses FindCursorCtl instead of* FindDItem, since FindDItem was actually forcing inactive edit line* items to become active.** Also, we only show an I-Beam over the an edit-line item with an* *active* Line Edit record, not over all the edit line items.** 4-Jun-91	Dave Lyons** Adding conditional code to use colorful icons, instead of black-and-white* ones (Note, Caution, Stop icons).  I need separate icons for 320 vs. 640.** 10-Jun-91	Dave Lyons** Removed check for an editLine item being active; we use the I-Beam cursor* over even inactive ones now.** Exported colored icons so the ROM 3 patch can use them.** 26-Aug-91	Dave Lyons** Added check in CreateIcon for dialog at odd X position.  If odd,* we make the icon position (local coordinates) odd too, so the colors* will be right.** 13-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** In 320 mode, NoteAlert, StopAlert, and CautionAlert were putting* their icons at X=0 instead of X=20.  Oops, fixed.** 5-Feb-92	Dave Lyons** Version $0304.************************************************************************* BEGIN 6.0.1** 26-Jan-93	Dave Lyons** Version $8305.  Removed a bogus DEY in Beep that was seeing the* high byte of the DAFont and deciding that a NIL sound proc was* actually non-nil, and calling it.  This was not a problem in ROM* 3, because it was already patched so that the sound proc is* always non-nil.** 1-Apr-93	Steve Stephenson** Version $0305 for 6.0.1 (final)***********************************************************************	blanks off	string asisTheDialogVersionNum	equ $0305	;1-Apr-93 SSColorIcons	equ 1	include 'all.macros'	include 'special.macros'	longa on	longi on	macro&lab	pushworddp &blah&lab	pei &blah	mend	macro&lab	pushlongdp &blah&lab	pei &blah+2	pei &blah	mend	MACRO	PushZPtr &A	pea  $0000	tdc	clc	adc  #&A	pha	MEND; *      copy  MemEqu.asm**********************************************************************************        Memory Manager Equates:**              Constants and Internal Structures	  ********************************************************************************** General Constants*nil	equ 0	Nil pointer valuetrue	equ $FFFF	Boolean truefalse	equ $0000	Boolean false;*;* Bank E1 memory equates;* addresses $E115AA - $E11AFF are reserved for the memory manager;*;MMRam	equ $E115AA	Beginning of our ram;MMRamEnd	equ $E11AFF	Last byte of our ram;;* Pointers to segment lists;*;MemList	equ $E11600	List of used segments;PurgeList	equ $E11604	List of used but empty handles;FreeList	equ $E11608	List of free handles;Mem01	equ $E1160C	Begining of bank 1;MemE0	equ $E11610	Begining of bank E0;MemFF	equ $E11614	Last segment;;* Other stuff;*;DoMove	equ $E11618	Code that does block move;NumBanks	equ $E1161C	Number of 64K banks	in machine;;		not counting E0, E1;HandleBuf	equ $E11700	$E11700 - $E1AFF is	used for handles** Zero page stuff*error	equ 1	Error codeaddr	equ error+2Count	equ addrattr	equ addr+4Dest	equ attr	Block Move Destinationowner	equ attr+2size	equ owner+2Source	equ sizehndl1	equ size+4TempCount	equ hndl1hndl2	equ hndl1+4hndl	equ hndl2+4addr1	equ hndl+4addr2	equ addr1+4ZPSize	equ addr2+4-1	# bytes we're adding to stacknumparms	equ addr2+4return	equ numparms+2	Users 2 return addressesparms	equ return+6	Parameters start here* Parameters and function results*ParmHndl	equ parms	Inputted handle for	most callsResHndl	equ parms+12	Handle returned by newhandle;		and handle inputted	by reallochandle* End of zero page stuff** The handle data structure*Hndl_Addr	equ 0	4 byte address pointed to by handleHndl_Attr	equ 4	2 byte attributes byteHndl_Owner	equ 6	2 byte segment owner IDHndl_Size	equ 8	4 byte sizeHndl_Prev	equ 12	4 byte pointer to previous handleHndl_Next	equ 16	4 byte pointer to next handleHSize	equ 20	Size of handle data	structure* Handle attributes	bits*Attr_Locked	equ $8000	1 = LockedAttr_Fixed	equ $4000	1 = Not movableAttr_Purge	equ $0300	0 = No purge 1-3 purge levelAttr_NoCross	equ $0010	1 = May not cross banksAttr_NoSpec	equ $0008	1 = May not use special memoryAttr_Page	equ $0004	1 = Page AlignedAttr_Addr	equ $0002	1 = Fixed addressAttr_Bank	equ $0001	1 = Fixed address** Error codes*MFullErr	equ $0201	Memory full errorNilErr	equ $0202	Operation on a nil handleNotNilErr	equ $0203	Operation on a non nil handleLockErr	equ $0204	Operation on a locked blockPurgeErr	equ $0205	Attempt to purge unpurgeable blockHandleErr	equ $0206	Invalid handle inputted; *      copy  QdHeader.asm; QDHeader.asm	TITLE 'QuickDraw Header';++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;; Some Structures and Equates from QuickDraw;;++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;;;; +++ Paint Pixels parameter block ++++++++;PP_SrcInfo	equ 0PP_DesInfo	equ PP_SrcInfo+4PP_SrcRect	equ PP_DesInfo+4PP_DesRect	equ PP_SrcRect+4PP_Mode	equ PP_DesRect+4PP_Clip	equ PP_Mode+2;; +++ LocInfo record +++++++++++++++++;PortSCB	equ 0PixelImage	equ PortSCB+2Width	equ PixelImage+4PBounds	equ Width+2LOCINFO	equ PBounds+8;; +++++ Region record +++++;Rgn_Len	equ 0Rgn_Bounds	equ Rgn_Len+2;;; +++++ Port record	+++++;GP_PortInfo	equ 0GP_Bounds	equ GP_PortInfo+8GP_PortRect	equ GP_Bounds+8GP_ClipRgn	equ GP_PortRect+8GP_VisRgn	equ GP_ClipRgn+4GP_BkPat	equ GP_VisRgn+4;PORTSIZE	EQU 186;; +++++ Rectangle Structure +++++;y1	EQU 0x1	EQU y1+2y2	EQU x1+2x2	EQU y2+2RECTSIZE	EQU x2+2;; *** window parameter block for _NewWindow ***;templ_len	equ 0wind_frame	equ templ_len+2wind_title	equ wind_frame+2wind_ref	equ wind_title+4wind_full	equ wind_ref+4wind_clr	equ wind_full+8wind_voff	equ wind_clr+4wind_hoff	equ wind_voff+2wind_datah	equ wind_hoff+2wind_dataw	equ wind_datah+2wind_max_h	equ wind_dataw+2wind_max_w	equ wind_max_h+2wind_vscrl	equ wind_max_w+2	Number of pixels to	scroll vertically.wind_hscrl	equ wind_vscrl+2	Number of pixels to	scroll horizontally.wind_vpage	equ wind_hscrl+2	Number of pixels to	page vertically.wind_hpage	equ wind_vpage+2	Number of pixels to	page horizontally.wind_infot	equ wind_hpage+2	Infomation bar text	string.wind_infoh	equ wind_infot+4	Height of information barwind_def	equ wind_infoh+2	DefProc.wind_info	equ wind_def+4	Routine to draw info. bar.wind_draw	equ wind_info+4	Routine to draw content.wind_pos	equ wind_draw+4	Size/Position of content.wind_plane	equ wind_pos+8	Plane to put window	up in.wind_rec	equ wind_plane+4	Address of memory for window record.;; Icon Item Template;IconitemID	equ 0IconitemRect	equ IconitemID+2IconitemType	equ IconitemRect+8IconitemDescr	equ IconitemType+2IconitemValue	equ IconitemDescr+4IconitemFlag	equ IconitemValue+2IconitemColor	equ IconitemFlag+2;; *      copy  EvHeader.asm; EvHeader.asm	TITLE 'Event Manager Header';+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;; Structures and Equates for the Event Manager;;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;; +++++ Event Structure +++++;what	equ 0message	equ what+2when	equ message+4where	equ when+4modif	equ where+4evtsize	equ modif+2TaskData	equ modif+2	when using TaskMasterTaskMask	equ TaskData+4	events to be handled by TaskMaster;;; --- Event codes ----------------------------------------;inNull	equ $00	No further action required.inButtDwn	equ $01	Button down event.inButtUp	equ $02	Button up event.inKey	equ $03	Key event.;              $04		(Not defined.)inAutoKey	equ $05	Auto-Key event.inUpdate	equ $06	Update event.;              $07		(Not defined.)inActWind	equ $08	Activate window event.inSwitch	equ $09	Switch event.inAccess	equ $0A	Desk Accessory event.inDevice	equ $0B	Device driver event.;              $0C		Application defined.;              $0D		Application defined.;              $0E		Application defined.;              $0F		Application defined.;;; --- Modifier key flags --------------------------------;K_KEYPAD	equ $2000K_CTRL	equ $1000K_OPTION	equ $0800K_CAPSLOCK	equ $0400K_SHIFT	equ $0200K_COMMAND	equ $0100K_BUTT0	equ $0080K_BUTT1	equ $0040K_CHANGE	equ $0002K_ACTIVE	equ $0001;;; --- These are values returned by FindWindow and TaskMaster,    ------; --- and may mean different things depending on who returns it. ------;inDesk	equ $10	On the desktop.inSysMenu	equ $11	In system menu barinSysWind	equ $12	In system window (desk accessory).inContent	equ $13	In a content region.inDrag	equ $14	In a drag region.inGrow	equ $15	In a grow (size) region.inGoAway	equ $16	In a go-away (close	box) region.inZoom	equ $17	In a zoom (zoom box) region.inInfo	equ $18	In the information bar.inVerScrl	equ $19	In the vertical scroll bar.inHorScrl	equ $1A	In the horizontal scroll bar.inFrame	equ $1B	On a window frame, other than above.inDrop	equ $1C	On a window drop shadow.;;; *      copy  WHeader.asm; WHEADER.ASM	               D. Oliver;; Structures and Equates for Cortland Window Manager.;;;; +++ Window structure and equates ++++++++++++++++++++++++++;;          Copyright Apple Computer, Inc.1986-88.  All Rights Reserved ;                Written by Dan Oliver;          *** C O N F I D E N T I A L ***;;;wnext	equ 0	Pointer to next window, 0=bottom.wport	equ wnext+4	Window's port.wstrucRgn	equ wport+PORTSIZE	Handle of window's entire region.wcontRgn	equ wstrucRgn+4	Handle of window's content region.wupdateRgn	equ wcontRgn+4	Handle of area needing to be redrawn.wcontrol	equ wupdateRgn+4	Pointer to controls	in window.wFrameCtrl	equ wcontrol+4	Pointer to controls	in frame.;wframe	equ wFrameCtrl+4	Type of window, frame flags.wtitle	equ wframe+2	Pointer to window's title.wrefCon	equ wtitle+4	Reserved for application.wfull	equ wrefCon+4	Size of window, used with ZoomWindow.wcolor	equ wfull+8	Pointer to window's color table.y_origin	equ wcolor+4	Content's vertical offset.x_origin	equ y_origin+2	Content's horizontal offset.data_h	equ x_origin+2	Height of total data area.data_w	equ data_h+2	Width of total data	area.wmaxheight	equ data_w+2	Maximum height for grow window.wmaxwidth	equ wmaxheight+2	Maximum width for grow window.vscroll	equ wmaxwidth+2	Amount to scroll vertically (arrows).hscroll	equ vscroll+2	Amount to scroll horizonally (arrows).vpage	equ hscroll+2	Amount to page vertically (page region).hpage	equ vpage+2	Amount to page horizontally (page rgn).wInfoText	equ hpage+2	Value passed to Draw Info routine.wInfoHeight	equ wInfoText+4wdefProc	equ wInfoHeight+2	Window's definition procedure.wInfoDraw	equ wdefProc+4	Address of routine to draw Info Bar.updateDraw	equ wInfoDraw+4	Address of routine to draw content region.;wtitle_w	equ updateDraw+4	Width of title in pixels.woldYOrg	equ wtitle_w+2	Save y origin on full window.woldXOrg	equ woldYOrg+2	Save x origin on full window.worgn_mask	equ woldXOrg+2WINDSIZE	equ worgn_mask+2	Total size of a standard window structure.;;;; +++++ Window coordinate offsets +++++;TITLEH	EQU 13	Height of title bar.TITLEL	EQU 2	Space on left and right of title bar pattern.TITLET	EQU 3	Space on top and bottom of title bar pattern.;CLOSEL	EQU 10	Left side of window	to left side of close box.CLOSET	EQU 2	Top of window to top of close box.CLOSEW	EQU 22	Width of close box.CLOSEH	EQU 11	Height of close box.;;; --- Flag masks for wkind ------------------------------;W_SYSTEM	equ $8000	1 = system window.;;; --- Window Frame Type Masks ----------------------;F_TITLE	equ $8000	TRUE = title bar.F_CLOSE	equ $4000	TRUE = close box.F_ALERT	equ $2000	TRUE = alert frame.F_RSCRL	equ $1000	TRUE = right scroll	bar.F_BSCRL	equ $0800	TRUE = bottom scroll bar.F_GROW	equ $0400	TRUE = sizer box.F_ZOOM	equ $0100	TRUE = full box.F_MOVE	equ $0080	TRUE = allow move on title bar.F_VIS	equ $0020	TRUE = window is visible.F_INFO	equ $0010	TRUE = content inset from left side.F_CTRL_TIE	equ $0008	TRUE = controls not	tied to windowF_ALLOCATE	equ $0004	TRUE = window record allocated by me.F_ZOOMED	equ $0002	TRUE = window is currently zoomedF_HILITED	equ $0001	TRUE = frame is highlighted.;;; --- Window color table offsets -----------------------------;FRAME_CLR	EQU 0	Frame's outline.TITLE_CLR	EQU FRAME_CLR+2	Title's color.BAR_CLR	EQU TITLE_CLR+2	Title bar's initerior.GROW_CLR	EQU BAR_CLR+2	Grow box interior.INFOR_CLR	EQU GROW_CLR+2	Information bar interior.COLORSIZ	EQU INFOR_CLR+2	Size of color table.;WindToolNum	equ 14;; --- Variation code, command to window	definition procedure ----------;wDraw	equ 0	Draw window's frame.wHit	equ 1	Tell what region given point is in.wCalcRgns	equ 2	Calculate wstrucRgn	and wcontRgn.wNew	equ 3	Do any additional initialization.wDispose	equ 4	Take any additional	disposal actions.wGrow	equ 5	Draw window's grow image.;; --- Hit return flags -------------------------------------------------;Null	equ 0wInDesk	equ $10	On Desktop.wInMenuBar	equ $11	On System Menu Bar.wInSysWindow	equ $12	On System window.winContent	equ $13	In content region.wInDrag	equ $14	In drag region.wInGrow	equ $15	In grow region, active window only.wInGoAway	equ $16	In go-away region, active window only.wInZoom	equ $17	In zoom region, active window only.wInInfo	equ $18	In information bar.wInVScroll	equ $19	In right scroll bar.wInHScroll	equ $1A	In bottom scroll bar.wInFrame	equ $1B	In frame, but not on anything else.;;;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;          Drawing Equates;;          Copyright 1986 Apple Computer, Inc.;                Written by Dan Oliver;          *** C O N F I D E N T I A L ***;;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;;BLACK	EQU $0000RED	EQU $1111GREEN	EQU $2222BLUE	EQU $3333TEAL	EQU $4444COLOR5	EQU $5555BROWN	EQU $6666DKGRAY	EQU $7777LTGRAY	EQU $8888ORANGE	EQU $9999COLOR10	EQU $aaaaCOLOR11	EQU $bbbbYELLOW	EQU $ccccMAGENTA	EQU $ddddCYAN	EQU $eeeeWHITE	EQU $ffff;; +++ Pattern types	+++;P_SOLID	EQU $0000P_DITHER	EQU $0100P_DOTTED	EQU $0200P_LINED	EQU $0300;;; *      copy  CHeader.asm; CHEADER.ASM	               D. Oliver;	TITLE 'CHEADER.ASM';; Structures and Equates for Cortland Control Manager.;;;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;        Offsets for control structures.;;          Copyright 1986 Apple Computer, Inc.;                Written by Dan Oliver;          *** C O N F I D E N T I A L ***;;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;;; +++ General control header +++;CtrlNext	equ 0CtrlOwner	equ CtrlNext+4CtrlRect	equ CtrlOwner+4CtrlFlag	equ CtrlRect+RECTSIZECtrlHilite	equ CtrlFlag+1CtrlValue	equ CtrlHilite+1CtrlProc	equ CtrlValue+2CtrlAction	equ CtrlProc+4CtrlData	equ CtrlAction+4CtrlrefCon	equ CtrlData+4CtrlColor	equ CtrlrefCon+4Thumb	equ CtrlColor+4PageRegion	equ Thumb+RECTSIZE;;; --- CtrlFlag bit flags --------------------;C_HILITE	equ $FF00	Hilited part, 255 =	inactive.UP_FLAG	equ $0001	Up arrow.DOWN_FLAG	equ $0002	Down arrow.LEFT_FLAG	equ $0004	Left arrow.RIGHT_FLAG	equ $0008	Right arrow.DIR_SCROLL	equ $0010	0 = vertical, 1 = horizontal scroll.CTRL_INVIS	equ $0080	1 if control is invisible.FAMILY	equ $007F	family number for radio buttonsBOLD_BUTT	equ $0001	1 if thick outline for buttonNO_BOLD_BUTT	equ $FFFE	equals (not BOLD_BUTT);;; --- Task numbers ----------------------------;drawCntl	equ 0	Draw the control.calcCRect	equ drawCntl+1	Compute the drag RECT.testCntl	equ calcCRect+1	Perform a hit test on the control.initCntl	equ testCntl+1	Perform additional initialization.dispCntl	equ initCntl+1	Perform additional disposal.posCntl	equ dispCntl+1	Called when dragging complete with delta.thumbCntl	equ posCntl+1	Setup for dragging.dragCntl	equ thumbCntl+1	Perform dragging.autoTrack	equ dragCntl+1	Called while dragging.newValue	equ autoTrack+1	Called when new value is set.setParams	equ newValue+1	Called when min and	max are set.moveCntl	equ setParams+1	Move entire control.recSize	equ moveCntl+1	Return size of control's record.;;; --- Part codes for standard controls -----------------;BUTT_PART	equ 2CHECK_PART	equ 3UP_PART	equ 5DOWN_PART	equ 6UPP_PART	equ 7DOWNP_PART	equ 8GROW_PART	equ 10THUMB_PART	equ 129;CtrlToolNum	equ 16;;; --- Control icon numbers -------------------------------;UP_ARROW	equ 8DOWN_ARROW	equ 10LEFT_ARROW	equ 12RITE_ARROW	equ 14GROW_ICON	equ 16;TITLE_SPACE	equ 4	Number of pixels added to the width of;	                   a check box or radio	button to get the;	                   starting X position of the title.;; *      copy  CHeader.asm; CHEADER.ASM	               D. Oliver;	TITLE 'CHEADER.ASM';; Structures and Equates for Cortland Control Manager.;;;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;        Offsets for control structures.;;          Copyright 1986 Apple Computer, Inc.;                Written by Dan Oliver;          *** C O N F I D E N T I A L ***;;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;;; +++ General control header +++;; --- CtrlFlag bit flags --------------------;;; --- Task numbers ----------------------------;; --- Control icon numbers -------------------------------;;	                   a check box or radio	button to get the;	                   starting X position of the title.;; *      copy  DHeader.asm; DHeader.asm		Jean-Charles Mourey	TITLE 'Dialog Manager Equates';++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;; Structure and Equates for the Cortland Dialog Manager;;++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;=======================================================;;   * * *  P U B L I C   E Q U A T E S	* * *;;=======================================================;; Dialog Manager Errors;DLGERR	equ $1500	; Error BaseDlgMgrAlreadyActive	equ 1DlgMgrNotActive	equ 2BadItemType	equ 10	; error number is DLGERR+WhichErrorNewItemFailed	equ 11ItemNotFound	equ 12NotModalDialog	equ 13	; Dialog is not modal;; Item Types;ButtonItem	equ 10CheckItem	equ 11RadioItem	equ 12ScrollBarItem	equ 13UserCtlItem	equ 14StatText	equ 15LongStatText	equ 16EditLine	equ 17IconItem	equ 18PicItem	equ 19UserItem	equ 20UserCtlItem2	equ 21LongStatText2	equ 22	;DAN H. (added new item)MinItemType	equ 10MaxItemType	equ 22	;DAN H. (to reflect	added item);; Part Code numbers	for non-standard control item;inStatText	equ 9inEditLine	equ 11inUserItem	equ 12inLongStatText	equ 13inIconItem	equ 14inLongStatText2	equ 15;; To disable an item for the dialog manager, add ItemDisable to the ItemType;ItemDisable	equ $8000;; Icon structure;;   - An Icon Handle is a handle to an Icon Record;   - The definition of an Icon Record follows:;iconRect	equ 0	; width must be multiple of 8iconImage	equ iconRect+RECTSIZE ; pixel image for	the icon;; Command Number for the Dialog Scroll Bar Action Procedure;getinitview	equ 1getinittotal	equ 2getinitvalue	equ 3scrolllineup	equ 4scrolllinedown	equ 5scrollpageup	equ 6scrollpagedown	equ 7scrollthumb	equ 8;; Item Template;ititemID	equ 0ititemRect	equ ititemID+2ititemType	equ ititemRect+8ititemDescr	equ ititemType+2ititemValue	equ ititemDescr+4ititemFlag	equ ititemValue+2ititemColor	equ ititemFlag+2;; Modal Dialog Template;dtBoundsRect	equ 0dtVisible	equ dtBoundsRect+8dtRefCon	equ dtVisible+2dtitemlist	equ dtRefCon+4;; ditemlist is a list of pointers to item templates terminated by a nil pointer;;; Alert Template;atBoundsRect	equ 0atalertID	equ atBoundsRect+8atstage1	equ atalertID+2atstage2	equ atstage1+1atstage3	equ atstage2+1atstage4	equ atstage3+1atitemlist	equ atstage4+1;; Additional Parameter Block for a UserCtlItem2;DefProcParm	equ 0	; custom control defprocTitleParm	equ 4	; control title (CtrlData)ParamLong	equ 8	; equivalent to Param1, Param2;=======================================================;;   * * *  P R I V A T E   E Q U A T E S  * * *;;=======================================================;; Dialog Record:;dwind	equ 0	; dialog windowdlgtype	equ dwind+WINDSIZE	; Modal, Modeless,...edittextID	equ dlgtype+2	; editText currently being editeddefbutID	equ edittextID+2	; default buttonDLGSIZE	equ defbutID+2	; size of dialog record;; Possible Dialog Types:;No_Type	equ 0Modal_Type	equ 1Modeless_Type	equ 2;; Standard Windows for Dialogs;DocProcID	equ 0	; standard document	windowDlgProcID	equ 1	; dialog (modal-type) window;; Dialog Manager Tool Number;DLGTOOL	equ $15	; Dialog Manager is	Tool #21;; Command Number for cut/copy/paste/delete commands (in dscrap.asm);cutcmd	equ 0copycmd	equ 1pastecmd	equ 2deletecmd	equ 3;; Icon IDs for alerts;stopIcon	equ 1noteIcon	equ 2cautionIcon	equ 3;; Icon Size in 320 and 640 mode;Icon320Width	equ 24Icon640Width	equ 40IconHeight	equ 18;; ItemStructure = Control Structure with RefCon = (ID, Type);iitemcontrol	equ 0iitemid	equ CtrlRefConiitemtype	equ iitemid+2STDCTRLSIZE	equ CtrlColor+4	; Std Ctrl Size (without add. datas);; Additional datas for StatText:;iitemfont	equ iitemcontrol+STDCTRLSIZEiitemface	equ iitemfont+4StatTextSIZE	equ iitemface+2LongStatTextSIZE	equ StatTextSIZE;; Additional datas for EditLine:;EditLineSIZE	equ STDCTRLSIZE	; no additional datas;; Additional datas for ScrollBar (in addition to the standard add. datas):;iScrollBarDef	equ PageRegion+RECTSIZE ; scroll bar item defproc pointerScrollBarSIZE	equ iScrollBarDef+4;; Additional datas for UserItem:;UserItemSIZE	equ STDCTRLSIZE;; Additional datas for IconItem:;IconItemSIZE	equ STDCTRLSIZE;; Dialog Signature;DlgSig	equ $2348;; Zero Page (shared	with Control Manager);Signature	equ 128	; contains DlgSig if Dlg Mgr activemmgrID	equ Signature+2	; ID to use with the Memory ManagerDialogFont	equ mmgrID+2	; handle to dialog font or 0 for systemAlertSoundProc	equ DialogFont+4	; pointer to custom	sound procedureAlertStage	equ AlertSoundProc+4 ; current alert stageLastAlertID	equ AlertStage+2	; ID of last called	alertParamString0	equ LastAlertID+2	; Param strings for	^0 to ^3ParamString1	equ ParamString0+4ParamString2	equ ParamString1+4ParamString3	equ ParamString2+4PartCodeHit	equ ParamString3+4	; Part Code HitMemHandle	equ PartCodeHit+2WindowPointer	equ MemHandle+4HandStruct	equ WindowPointer+4***EndZeroPage	equ HandStruct+4IBeamFlag	equ HandStruct+4	;5-Mar-91 DAL: nonzero = we called IBeamCursorEndZeroPage	equ IBeamFlag+2	;5-Mar-91 DAL************************************************************************ Forward References***********************************************************************	ENTRY DialogBootInit	ENTRY DialogStartup	ENTRY DialogShutDown	ENTRY DialogVersion	ENTRY DialogReset	ENTRY DialogStatus	ENTRY SetDAFont	ENTRY ErrorSound	ENTRY NewModalDialog	ENTRY NewModelessDialog	ENTRY CloseDialog	ENTRY NewDItem	ENTRY RemoveItem	ENTRY ModalDialog	ENTRY IsDialogEvent	ENTRY DialogSelect	ENTRY DlgCut	ENTRY DlgCopy	ENTRY DlgPaste	ENTRY DlgDelete	ENTRY DrawDialog	ENTRY Alert	ENTRY StopAlert	ENTRY NoteAlert	ENTRY CautionAlert	ENTRY ParamText	ENTRY SetDAFont	ENTRY SetItemToControl	ENTRY GetControlDItem	ENTRY SetIText	ENTRY HideDItem	ENTRY ShowDItem	ENTRY FindDItem	ENTRY UpdateDialog	ENTRY SetItemType	ENTRY GetItemBox	ENTRY SetItemBox	ENTRY GetFirstItem	ENTRY GetNextItem	ENTRY ModalDialog2	ENTRY RESERVED	ENTRY GetItemValue	ENTRY SetItemValue	ENTRY RESERVED	ENTRY RESERVED	ENTRY GetNewModalDialog	ENTRY GetNewDItem	ENTRY GetAlertStage	ENTRY ResetAlertStage	ENTRY DefaultFilter	ENTRY GetDefButton	ENTRY DisableDItem	ENTRY EnableDItem	ENTRY GetIText	ENTRY SelIText	ENTRY SetDefButton	ENTRY StdFilterProc	ENTRY GetItemType	ENTRY InsertParamString	ENTRY disposelocals	ENTRY DlgScrap	ENTRY dlg2handle	ENTRY scroll_action	ENTRY BlinkCaret	ENTRY WindowIsDialog	ENTRY EnableDisableItem	ENTRY ShowHideDItem	ENTRY quit10	ENTRY quit8	ENTRY FindNextEditLine	ENTRY quit6	ENTRY EmptyString	ENTRY long_call	ENTRY StdSoundProc	ENTRY GeneralAlert	ENTRY DialogFromTemplate	ENTRY quit4	ENTRY EmptyRect	ENTRY getWORDfromZP	ENTRY storeLONGinZP	ENTRY quit2	ENTRY NormalTextColor;====================================;        Install Dialog Manager;====================================	EXPORT DialogCallTableDialogCallTable	PROC	longa on	longi on	ENTRY FPTFPT	DC.L (ENDFPT-FPT)/4	DC.L DialogBootInit-1 1	DC.L DialogStartup-1 2	DC.L DialogShutDown-1 3	DC.L DialogVersion-1 4	DC.L DialogReset-1	5	DC.L DialogStatus-1	6	DC.L ErrorSound-1	7      ; should be RESERVED	DC.L SetDAFont-1	8      ; should be RESERVED	DC.L ErrorSound-1	9	DC.L NewModalDialog-1 10	DC.L NewModelessDialog-1 11	DC.L CloseDialog-1	12	DC.L NewDItem-1	13	DC.L RemoveItem-1	14	DC.L ModalDialog-1	15	DC.L IsDialogEvent-1 16	DC.L DialogSelect-1	17	DC.L DlgCut-1	18	DC.L DlgCopy-1	19	DC.L DlgPaste-1	20	DC.L DlgDelete-1	21	DC.L DrawDialog-1	22	DC.L Alert-1	23	DC.L StopAlert-1	24	DC.L NoteAlert-1	25	DC.L CautionAlert-1	26	DC.L ParamText-1	27	DC.L SetDAFont-1	28	DC.L SetItemToControl-1 29	DC.L GetControlDItem-1 30	DC.L GetIText-1	31	DC.L SetIText-1	32	DC.L SelIText-1	33	DC.L HideDItem-1	34	DC.L ShowDItem-1	35	DC.L FindDItem-1	36	DC.L UpdateDialog-1	37	DC.L GetItemType-1	38	DC.L SetItemType-1	39	DC.L GetItemBox-1	40	DC.L SetItemBox-1	41	DC.L GetFirstItem-1	42	DC.L GetNextItem-1	43	DC.L ModalDialog2-1	44	DC.L RESERVED-1	45	DC.L GetItemValue-1	46	DC.L SetItemValue-1	47	DC.L RESERVED-1	48	DC.L RESERVED-1	49	DC.L GetNewModalDialog-1 50	DC.L GetNewDItem-1	51	DC.L GetAlertStage-1 52	DC.L ResetAlertStage-1 53	DC.L DefaultFilter-1 54	DC.L GetDefButton-1	55	DC.L SetDefButton-1	56	DC.L DisableDItem-1	57	DC.L EnableDItem-1	58ENDFPT	ENDP;;            copy  DlgInit.asm; DlgInit.asm		Jean-Charles Mourey	TITLE 'Dialog Manager Initialization Routines';______________________________________________________________________________;;        DialogBootInit;;       input: none;;      output: none;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY DialogBootInitDialogBootInit	PROC	lda #0	clc	rtl	ENDP;______________________________________________________________________________;;        DialogStartup;;       input: ProgramID:WORD - ID to use with the Memory Manager;;      output: none;; Change History;; 4 Mar 88	Steven Glass;; Modified code to use the WAP entry for this tool.  First, we check the; WAP to see if we are already active.  If we are already active, then we; return a new error code.  If we are not active, we get the control; manager's direct page and save it in our WAP.;; 19 May 89	Steven Glass;; Changed it again so that we don't check to see if we were already active.; The march 4 check that is in ROM, doesn't work.  Anyway, we found that ; applications were dieing if an error was returned anyway.;;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY DialogStartupDialogStartup	PROC Export	tlink 2ProgramID	equ input;; Save ProgramID on	stack;	pei <ProgramIDNotYetActive;; Get Dialog Manager Zero Page;	pha	_GetCtlDPage	pld;; Set Dialog Mgr's WAP;	PushWord #0	PushWord #DlgTool	PushWord #0	phd	_SetWAP;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Now, using our part of the zero page, lets ; init our stuff.;	pla	; save memory manager ID to use	sta <mmgrID	lda #DlgSig	; Set signature	sta <Signature	zero #EndZeroPage-DialogFont,<DialogFont ; clear all other parms	pha	; long space for result	pha	pea 0	; get size of memory 	pushword #98	pei mmgrID;; was:;	pushword #0	; no restrictions	pea $4000	; allocate as fixed (non-moveable)		; cause we dereference it right away...	pha	pha	_NewHandle	pla	sta <MemHandle	pla	sta <MemHandle+2	lda [<MemHandle]	sta <WindowPointer	ldy #2	lda [<MemHandle],y	sta <WindowPointer+2	lda <WindowPointer	clc	adc #78	sta <HandStruct	lda <WindowPointer+2	adc #0	sta <HandStruct+2	lda #0000	ldx #0	; accumulator is already 0	jmp quit2	ENDP;_____________________________________________________________________________;;        ErrorSound;;       input: soundProc:LONG - pointer	to a sound procedure;;      output: none;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY ErrorSoundErrorSound	PROC	ldy #AlertSoundProc	jmp storeLONGinZP	ENDP;______________________________________________________________________________;;        SetDAFont;;       input: fontHandle:LONG - handle	of font;;      output: none;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY SetDAFontSetDAFont	PROC	ldy #DialogFont	jmp storeLONGinZP	ENDP;______________________________________________________________________________;;        DialogVersion;;       input: none;;      output: dVersion:WORD - Dialog Manager's version number;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY DialogVersionDialogVersion	PROCdVersion	equ 7	; stack relative	lda #TheDialogVersionNum	sta dVersion,s	lda #0	clc	rtl	ENDP;______________________________________________________________________________;;        DialogShutDown;;       input: none;;      output: none;; Change History;; 4 March 88	Steven Glass;; Modified to use the WAP instead of calling control manager.  Sets WAP to; zero when complete.;;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY DialogShutDownDialogShutDown	PROC	cmp #0	bne YesWeAreActive	lda #DlgErr+DlgMgrNotActive	sec	rtlYesWeAreActive	phd	tcd;; Clear signature to mark the dialog manager inactive;	stz <Signature	pei <MemHandle+2	pei <MemHandle	_DisposeHandle	PushWord #0	PushWord #DlgTool	PushLong #0	_SetWap	pld	lda #0	clc	rtl	ENDP;______________________________________________________________________________;;        DialogReset;;       input: none;;      output: none;; Change History;; 4 March 88	Steven Glass;; Changed to check first to see if we are active.  If active, we shut down.; if not active, we do nothing.;;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY DialogResetDialogReset	PROC;; Check WAP.  Are we active?;	cmp #0	beq DoNothing	; no	_DialogShutdown	; yesDoNothing	lda #0	clc	rtl	ENDP;_____________________________________________________________________________;;        DialogStatus;;       input: none;;      output: status:WORD - TRUE if Dialog Manager is initialized;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY DialogStatusDialogStatus	PROC	DefineStackRTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3ActiveResult	word	cmp #0	bne AmActive	EXPORT FinishActiveFinishActive	sta ActiveResult,s	lda #0	clc	rtlAmActive	lda #True	bra FinishActive;	ldy #Signature;	jmp getWORDfromZP	ENDP;            copy  NewDlg.asm; NewDlg.asm		Jean-Charles Mourey	TITLE 'New Dialog Routines';+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;;        NewDialog;;       input: DialogVariable:LONG - pointer to variable to	store the dialog in;              dBoundsRect:LONG - size and position of dialog's content region;              dTitle:LONG - pointer to	string for dialog's title;              dDefProc:LONG - 0 for document, 1 for dialog, or procptr.;              dBehind:LONG - pointer to window the dialog should be behind.;              dFlag:WORD - bit vector describing the dialog's frame;              dRefCon:LONG - any value	you'd like to associate with the window.;              dFullSize:LONG - pointer	to RECT to be used as content's zoomed.;;      output: none;;    function: Creates a new dialog. DialogVariable contains 0 if error.;;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++	ENTRY NewDialogNewDialog	PROCDlgRecHdl	equ 0DlgRecPtr	equ DlgRecHdl+4theDialog	equ DlgRecPtr+4Globals	equ theDialog+4TheMemHandle	equ Globals+4WindParmPtr	equ TheMemHandle+4SizeLocals	equ WindParmPtr+4	link 30,SizeLocalsdFullSize	equ inputdRefCon	equ dFullSize+4dFlag	equ dRefCon+4dBehind	equ dFlag+2dDefProc	equ dBehind+4dTitle	equ dDefProc+4dBoundsRect	equ dTitle+4DialogVariable	equ dBoundsRect+4;; Create a new window for the Dialog;;; Get Memory Manager ID to use;	pha	_GetCtlDPage	pla	sta <Globals	stz <Globals+2		ldy #MemHandle	; get handle to memory obtained at startup time	lda [<Globals],y	sta <TheMemHandle	iny	iny	lda [<Globals],y	sta <TheMemHandle+2	ldy #4	; lock down the handle	lda [<TheMemHandle],y	ora #$8000	sta [<TheMemHandle],y	dey	dey	lda [<TheMemHandle],y ; dereference handle	sta <WindParmPtr+2	lda [<TheMemHandle]	sta <WindParmPtr		zero #78,[<WindParmPtr] ; zero out space reserved for window parameters	lda #78	; store total size of window parameters	in templ_len	sta [<WindParmPtr];; Allocate space for the DialogRecord;	pha	; space for handle	pha	pushlong #DLGSIZE	ldy #mmgrID	; Memory Manager ID	lda [<Globals],y	pha	pushword #Attr_Fixed+Attr_NoCross	pha	; no use for a Location paramter	pha	_NewHandle	Check_Error NotAllocated	pulllong <DlgRecHdl;; Zero Dialog Record;	movelong [<DlgRecHdl],0,<DlgRecPtr	zero #DLGSIZE,[<DlgRecPtr];; Store the input parameters in wind_param for NewWindow;;       movelong <DlgRecPtr,>wind_rec	lda <DlgRecPtr	ldy #wind_rec	sta [<WindParmPtr],y	lda <DlgRecPtr+2	iny	iny	sta [<WindParmPtr],y;       movelong [<dBoundsRect],0,>wind_pos	lda [<dBoundsRect]	ldy #wind_pos	sta [<WindParmPtr],y	ldy #2	lda [<dBoundsRect],y	ldy #wind_pos+2	sta [<WindParmPtr],y;       movelong [<dBoundsRect],4,>wind_pos+4	ldy #4	lda [<dBoundsRect],y	ldy #wind_pos+4	sta [<WindParmPtr],y	ldy #6	lda [<dBoundsRect],y	ldy #wind_pos+6	sta [<WindParmPtr],y;       movelong <dTitle,>wind_title	lda <dTitle	ldy #wind_title	sta [<WindParmPtr],y	lda <dTitle+2	iny	iny	sta [<WindParmPtr],y;       movelong <dBehind,>wind_plane	lda <dBehind	ldy #wind_plane	sta [<WindParmPtr],y	lda <dBehind+2	iny	iny	sta [<WindParmPtr],y	lda <dFlag	; I allocated the space	ora #F_ALLOCATE	ldy #wind_frame	sta [<WindParmPtr],y;       movelong <dRefCon,>wind_ref	lda <dRefCon	ldy #wind_ref	sta [<WindParmPtr],y	lda <dRefCon+2	iny	iny	sta [<WindParmPtr],y;       movelong [<dFullSize],0,>wind_full	lda [<dFullSize]	ldy #wind_full	sta [<WindParmPtr],y	ldy #2	lda [<dFullSize],y	ldy #wind_full+2	sta [<WindParmPtr],y;       movelong [<dFullSize],4,>wind_full+4	ldy #4	lda [<dFullSize],y	ldy #wind_full+4	sta [<WindParmPtr],y	ldy #6	lda [<dFullSize],y	ldy #wind_full+6	sta [<WindParmPtr],y;       movelong <dDefProc,>wind_def	lda <dDefProc	ldy #wind_def	sta [<WindParmPtr],y	lda <dDefProc+2	iny	iny	sta [<WindParmPtr],y;; Call NewWindow;	pha	; space for window ptr	pha	lda <WindParmPtr+2	pha	lda <WindParmPtr	pha	_NewWindow	Check_Error NotAllocated	pla	; store result in local var	sta <theDialog	; theDialog and in input parameter	sta [<DialogVariable] ; DialogVariable	pla	sta <theDialog+2	ldy #2	sta [<DialogVariable],y;; Initialize extra fields in dialog record;	lda #0	; ID of EditLine currently being edited	ldy #edittextID-wport	sta [<theDialog],y	lda #1	; default Button ID	ldy #defbutID-wport	sta [<theDialog],y;; Look if dialog font is system font or	custom font;	ldy #DialogFont	; if DialogFont Handle is zero, system	lda [<Globals],y	; font, else handle	to custom font	bne SetDialogFont	iny	lda [<Globals],y	beq NoError;; Set the dialog font to the current dialog manager font;SetDialogFont		; 	pha	; space for port pointer	pha	_GetPort	; port pointer is on stack	pushlongdp <theDialog	_SetPort	ldy #DialogFont+2	; push font handle	lda [<Globals],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<Globals],y	pha	_SetFont	_SetPort	; reset prev port (which is on stack)NoError		; 	lda #0	; no errorexit	tax	; save error message	ldy #4	; unlock TheMemHandle	lda [<TheMemHandle],y	and #$7FFF	sta [<TheMemHandle],y	txa	 	unlink	rtlNotAllocated		;	    ; Unable to allocate space	tax	; save error code	pla	; pull useless result	pla	lda #0	; clear result (dialog pointer = 0)	sta [<DialogVariable]	ldy #2	sta [<DialogVariable],y	txa	; restore error code	bra exit	; A contains error code	ENDP;______________________________________________________________________________;;        NewModalDialog;;       input: dBoundsRect:LONG - size and position of dialog's content region.;              dVisible:WORD - TRUE if dialog is visible, FALSE if invisible.;              dRefCon:LONG - any value	you'd like to associate with the window.;;      output: theDialog:LONG - pointer	to dialog port, zero if error.;;    function: Creates a dialog of type	modal. The memory is allocated.;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY NewModalDialogNewModalDialog	PROC	tlink 10dRefCon	equ inputdVisible	equ dRefCon+4dBoundsRect	equ dVisible+2theDialog	equ output;; Call NewDialog to	create the Dialog;	pushzptr <theDialog	; variable to store	result in	pushlongdp <dBoundsRect	lda #0	; no title	pha	; (pushlong #0)	pha	pha	; standard window	pha	dec a	; Modal Dialog is always frontmost	pha	; visible window	pha	; (pushlong #-1)	pushword #F_CTRL_TIE+F_ALERT	lda <dVisible	; set flag to visible state	beq pushotherparms	pla	; dialog is visible	ora #F_VIS	phapushotherparms	pushlongdp <dRefCon	pushlong #EmptyRect	; no Full Size for a modal dialog.	jsl NewDialog	bcs exit	; error!, exit;; Set Type of Dialog to Modal in dialog	record;	lda #Modal_Type	; type of dialog	ldy #dlgtype-wport	sta [<theDialog],y	lda #0	; no errorexit		; 	tunlink	rtl	ENTRY EmptyRectEmptyRect	DC.W 0,0,0,0	ENDP;______________________________________________________________________________;;        NewModelessDialog;;       input: dBoundsRect:LONG - size and position of dialog's content region.;              dTitle:LONG - pointer to	string for dialog's title;              dBehind:LONG - pointer to window the dialog should be behind.;              dFlag:WORD - bit vector describing the dialog's frame;              dRefCon:LONG - any value	you'd like to associate with the window.;              dFullSize:LONG - pointer	to RECT to be used as content's zoomed.;;      output: theDialog:LONG - pointer	to dialog port, zero if error.;;    function: Creates a dialog of type	modal. The memory is allocated.;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY NewModelessDialogNewModelessDialog	PROC	tlink 22dFullSize	equ inputdRefCon	equ dFullSize+4dFlag	equ dRefCon+4dBehind	equ dFlag+2dTitle	equ dBehind+4dBoundsRect	equ dTitle+4theDialog	equ output;; Call NewDialog to	create the Dialog;	pushzptr <theDialog	; variable to store	result in	pushlongdp <dBoundsRect	pushlongdp <dTitle	pushlong #0	; standard window	pushlongdp <dBehind	pushworddp <dFlag	pushlongdp <dRefCon	pushlongdp <dFullSize	jsl NewDialog	bcs exit	; error!, exit;; Set Type of Dialog to Modeless in dialog record;	lda #Modeless_Type	; type of dialog	ldy #dlgtype-wport	sta [<theDialog],y	lda #0	; no errorexit		; 	tunlink	rtl	ENDP;______________________________________________________________________________;;        CloseDialog;;       input: theDialog:LONG - pointer	to the dialog;;      output: none.;;    function: removes the dialog from the screen, deletes it from the window;              list, and releases the memory occupied by the itemlist and the;              dialogrecord.;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY CloseDialogCloseDialog	PROC*** 7-Mar-91 DAL: If we left the cursor an I-Beam, make it an arrow when the dialog closes	pha	tax	lda >IBeamFlag,x	beq @notIBeam	lda #0	sta >IBeamFlag,x	_InitCursor@notIBeam	pla	;get WAP back*** end of 7-Mar-91 DAL	tlink 4;; CloseWindow removes the window from the screen and the window list,; and releases the memory occupied by the controllist (ie the itemlist); and by the dialog	record	pushlongdp <input	_CloseWindow	ldx #0	; no local space	jmp quit4	ENDP;______________________________________________________________________________;;        GetNewModalDialog;;       input: DialogTemplate:LONG - pointer to Dialog Template;;      output: theDialog:LONG - pointer	to dialog port, zero if error;______________________________________________________________________________	ENTRY GetNewModalDialogGetNewModalDialog	PROC	tlink 4DialogTemplate	equ inputtheDialog	equ output;; Call DialogFromTemplate to create dialog;	pushzptr <theDialog	pushlongdp <DialogTemplate ; pointer to template	ldy #dtVisible	; Visible parameter	lda [<DialogTemplate],y	pha	pushlong [<DialogTemplate],dtRefCon ; RefCon parameter	lda #dtitemlist	; offset to item list	pha	jsl DialogFromTemplate ; create dialog and set error status	ldx #0	jmp quit4	ENDP;++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++;;        DialogFromTemplate;;       input: DialogVariable:LONG - pointer to variable to	stock dialog in;              Template:LONG - pointer to template (dialog or alert);              Visible:WORD - visible parameter;              RefCon:LONG - refcon parameter;              ItemListOffset:WORD - offset to item list in	template;           ;      output: none;;    function: create a modal dialog from a template (used by GetNewModalDialog;              and Alert) and set the error status.;;++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++	ENTRY DialogFromTemplateDialogFromTemplate	PROCtheDialog	equ 0ItemTemplate	equ theDialog+4SizeLocals	equ ItemTemplate+4	link 16,SizeLocalsItemListOffset	equ inputRefCon	equ ItemListOffset+2Visible	equ RefCon+4Template	equ Visible+2DialogVariable	equ Template+4;; First, creates a modal dialog;	pha	; space for dialog pointer	pha	pushlongdp <Template	; pointer to rectangle	pushworddp <Visible	; Visible parameter	pushlongdp <RefCon	; RefCon parameter	_NewModalDialog	Check_Error NotCreated	pla	; store result in local var	sta <theDialog	; theDialog and in input parameter	sta [<DialogVariable] ; DialogVariable	pla	sta <theDialog+2	ldy #2	sta [<DialogVariable],y;; Compute pointer to first item template;; Bug fix: Non zero	DRefCon caused crash because drefcon was added in. 11/5/87;         add4  <Template,<ItemListOffset,<ItemTemplate	   ;fixed DAN H.	lda <Template	clc	adc <ItemListOffset	sta <ItemTemplate	lda <Template+2	adc #0	sta <ItemTemplate+2;; Then, creates the	list of items;CreateItems;; First check that we are not at the end of the list;	lda [<ItemTemplate]	bne CreateOne	ldy #2	lda [<ItemTemplate],y	beq exit	; if beq, acc is already 0 (no error);; Create one item;CreateOne	pushlongdp <theDialog	ldy #2	lda [<ItemTemplate],y	pha	lda [<ItemTemplate]	pha	_GetNewDItem;; Get pointer to template of next item in the list;	add4 <ItemTemplate,#4,<ItemTemplate	bra CreateItemsexit	unlink	rtlNotCreated		; 	tax	; save error code	pla	; pull useless result	sta [<DialogVariable]	pla	ldy #2	sta [<DialogVariable],y	txa	; restore error code	bra exit	ENDP;            copy  Alert.asm; Alert.asm	            Jean-Charles Mourey	TITLE 'Alert Procedures';..............................................;;        Alert Icon	Datas;;..............................................	ENTRY AlertIconDatasAlertIconDatas	PROC export;   ENTRY  IconHandleStruct;IconHandleStruct	DS.B  20	    ; Fake Handle structure to icon	export Icon320TableIcon320Table	DC.L StopIcon320	DC.L NoteIcon320	DC.L CautionIcon320	export Icon640TableIcon640Table	DC.L StopIcon640	DC.L NoteIcon640	DC.L CautionIcon640;   ENTRY  Icon_Template;Icon_Template  DC.W    -32768	        ; item ID;               DC.W    5,20,23,60	        ; *** subject to change;               DC.W    IconItem+ItemDisa